# Palm Island #1 — HOOK / curl shape (52 × 20 × 11)
# An asymmetric island whose lower-right end curls upward into a hook,
# enclosing a small turquoise lagoon. Solid simple geometries, no
# isolated pixels. Palm trunks are 2x2 (rounded look), crowns are
# overlapping plus-shapes for organic feel.

material sand     top=#F4E0A0  front=#A89060  side=#705D40
material sandwet  top=#E8C880  front=#9C7E48  side=#6A5630
material grass    top=#5A8E32  front=#365A1E  side=#243D14
material trunk    top=#8C5A2E  front=#5A3818  side=#3A2410
material frond    top=#3FB048  front=#1E7028  side=#104818
material frondlt  top=#62E03A  front=#3A8E20  side=#2C7018
material coconut  top=#5A4030  front=#3A271A  side=#251910
material rock     top=#8E785A  front=#5C4F3D  side=#3F362A

# ============================================================================
# SAND FOOTPRINT — built from overlapping bands so the contour steps
# in/out organically rather than being rectangular.
# Layout: main body in the upper-left, hook arm curling down then right
# enclosing a central lagoon (which is left as plain water).
# ============================================================================

# --- Main body (upper-left lobe), broad and tall ---
box 11 1 8    24 1 16   sand
box 13 1 6    27 1 17   sand
box 16 1 5    30 1 17   sand
box 19 1 4    32 1 16   sand
box 22 1 5    33 1 14   sand

# --- Neck connecting to the hook arm ---
box 25 1 8    34 1 12   sand
box 27 1 9    35 1 11   sand

# --- Hook arm (curls down and to the right) ---
box 30 1 4    36 1 8    sand
box 33 1 3    38 1 7    sand
box 35 1 2    40 1 6    sand
box 37 1 3    42 1 5    sand
box 40 1 4    43 1 7    sand
box 41 1 5    43 1 9    sand   # tip curling up to enclose lagoon

# --- Lagoon (between body and hook arm) — leave as water/shallow ---
# (no sand placed at x=33..41, z=10..14)

# --- Wet-sand fringe along the lagoon edge ---
box 33 1 9    34 1 9    sandwet
box 35 1 9    35 1 9    sandwet
box 36 1 8    37 1 8    sandwet
box 41 1 10   42 1 12   sandwet
box 27 1 13   30 1 14   sandwet

# ============================================================================
# RAISED SAND y=2 — smaller, smoother island top
# ============================================================================
box 14 2 8    22 2 15   sand
box 17 2 7    27 2 16   sand
box 20 2 6    30 2 15   sand
box 22 2 7    31 2 13   sand

# Hook arm raised slightly
box 36 2 4    40 2 6    sand
box 37 2 5    39 2 5    sand

# ============================================================================
# GRASS plateau on the highest part
# ============================================================================
box 18 3 8    24 3 14   grass
box 20 3 9    26 3 13   grass
box 22 3 10   25 3 12   grass

# ============================================================================
# PALM TREES (trunk = 2x2 cross section, crown = overlapping + shape)
# Pattern: trunk box, then 2-layer canopy with extending arms, then top tuft.
# ============================================================================

# ---- Palm A: tall, on the main grass plateau ----
box 22 1 10   23 8 11   trunk
box 22 9 10   23 9 11   trunk
# Canopy (plus-shape, 2 layers)
box 19 9 10   26 9 11   frond
box 22 9 7    23 9 14   frond
box 21 10 10  24 10 11  frondlt
box 22 10 9   23 10 12  frondlt
v 22 11 10   frondlt
v 23 11 11   frondlt
# Coconuts at trunk top
v 21 8 10   coconut
v 24 8 11   coconut

# ---- Palm B: smaller, west side ----
box 14 1 10   15 6 11   trunk
box 12 7 10   17 7 11   frond
box 14 7 8    15 7 13   frond
box 13 8 10   16 8 11   frondlt
v 14 9 10   frondlt
v 15 9 11   frondlt
v 13 6 10   coconut

# ---- Palm C: leans over the lagoon edge (upper neck) ----
box 28 1 13   29 6 14   trunk
box 26 7 13   31 7 14   frond
box 28 7 11   29 7 16   frond
box 27 8 13   30 8 14   frondlt
v 28 9 13   frondlt
v 29 9 14   frondlt
v 30 6 13   coconut

# ---- Palm D: on the hook arm tip ----
box 38 1 4    39 5 5    trunk
box 36 6 4    41 6 5    frond
box 38 6 2    39 6 7    frond
box 37 7 4    40 7 5    frondlt
v 38 8 4   frondlt
v 39 8 5   frondlt

# ---- Palm E: small one on the inner curl of the hook ----
box 41 1 8    42 4 8    trunk
box 39 5 7   43 5 9    frond
box 41 5 6   42 5 10   frond
v 41 6 8   frondlt
v 42 6 8   frondlt

# ============================================================================
# A few rocks at the lagoon entrance (acts as a natural breakwater)
# ============================================================================
box 36 1 12   37 2 13   rock
box 39 1 9    40 1 10   rock

# Shoreline rocks on the outer (south) shore
box 18 1 4    19 1 4    rock
box 32 1 14   33 2 15   rock
